ries. Placing a stone there would complete the horizontal five-in-a-row and secure the win.\n\n**Evaluation of Candidate Moves:**\n\n*   **Move K8:** This move creates the winning five-in-a-row.\n*   **Move K9 and G9:** Both look interesting but are irrelevant, as K8 leads to an immediate win.\n\n**Decision**\n\nBlack has four stones in a row at G8, H8, I8, and J8. The position F8 is occupied by White.  Placing a stone at K8 creates a five-in-a-row, which is an immediate win. Therefore, my move will be K8.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation:\nThe board currently shows a critical formation for Black (X). Black has four stones lined up horizontally in Row 8 at G8, H8, I8, and J8. This is a "Four-in-a-Row" formation. One end of this line (F8) is blocked by a White stone, but the other end (K8) is empty.\n\nReason:\nThe primary goal of Gomoku is to connect 5 stones. Since Black already has 4 connected stones at G8, H8, I8, and J8, placing a stone at K8 will complete the line of 5 (G8, H8, I8, J8, K8). This is an immediate winning move. No other move needs to be considered as this secures victory instantly.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "K", "row": 8}'}
